   "answer": "**Avoid deadlock by ensuring that not all philosophers can hold one fork while waiting for the other.**  \n\n### Common fixes\n- **Limit concurrent diners** – allow at most 4 of the 5 philosophers to sit down; the fifth must wait, guaranteeing a free fork for someone to finish.  \n- **Atomic fork acquisition** – require a philosopher to pick up both forks in a single atomic operation; if both are unavailable, the philosopher waits without holding any fork.  \n\nBoth approaches break the circular‑wait condition, so a deadlock cannot form. [[3]]",
