   "category": "followup",
   "context": "4e55769a7a51779d",
   "answer": "No. Two‑phase locking ensures conflict‑serializable schedules, but it does not eliminate deadlocks; cycles can still form in the wait‑for graph and must be detected or avoided separately[[1]].",
